Z||000011||Seanh||06-19-2001||11:38 AM||||A 10" solobaric round or L7 square should fit without problems in your console. Since you don't cut out the speaker hole, you can cut a square one for your L7. Don't know if they have spec's on their website, but it can be found at: <A HREF="http://www.kicker.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kicker.com</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||AusFiero||06-19-2001||12:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Seanh:<BR><B>A 10" solobaric round or L7 square should fit without problems in your console. Since you don't cut out the speaker hole, you can cut a square one for your L7. Don't know if they have spec's on their website, but it can be found at: <A HREF="http://www.kicker.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kicker.com</A> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The kicker S10L7 10" would work great in the larger console size with no CD box. Based on their cubic feet requirements and mounting depth. Says it needs .66 cubic feet of box, my largest console has .61 cubic feet which is pretty close.<P>The kicker S8L7 8" would work in all size consoles based on the manufacturers recommended cubic air volume and mounting. Works in a box .3 cubic feet up to .7 cubic feet.<P>Look pretty good too don't they. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||grinthock||06-19-2001||06:45 PM||||Well I do'nt need the CD TRAY --- That's for sure, I have a visor and stuff like that...  If we removed the CD Tray, could we get .66 ? That's the smallest box sub apparantly...<P>Now let's CHECK all the specs...<P>Mounting Depth 6-1/4 inches<BR>it's a 9-1/2 hole square<P><BR>Think it will fit?    Aus you do'nt cut the hole?  We do?    Just making sure, also, if we have a 9.5 inch square sub is there gonna be enough stuff to hold it in from moving?  I am gonna do the 10"L7 DVC Kicker<BR> <A HREF="http://www.kicker.com/kcsc/mainx.closeup?p_menu=subwoofers&p_image=/images/2001/products/S10L7_WO.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kicker.com/kcsc/mainx.closeup?p_menu=subwoofers&p_image=/images/2001/products/S10L7_WO.jpg</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||grinthock||06-19-2001||07:07 PM||||<BR>HMMMMMM Might look nice....<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/crap2.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||AusFiero||06-20-2001||01:34 AM||||heheh grinthock...I was gunna do that last night. <P>Certainly a different look to your average sub isn't it.<P>To answer your question grinthock yes it will fit with plenty. of room to screw it in as the plate is approximately 11.5 inches. Tight fit yes, but a fit. I could possibly squeeze another 0.05 cubic feet out of the sub  box by making it a half inch deeper. Couldn't guarantee your elbow room but judging by my car I couldn't see any mayor problems. Although I think it would still work fine in a .6 box as the sub is only 6" from your right ear. <P>My specs said a box .5 to .7 I am running it in a .35 box and still get a good bass response after I fiddled with my stereo controls a little.<p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||14
